Subject: [PATCH 11/53] B70-IP-K6: CPU tests (spec/page, views, dequant math,
 interpreter kernels)

Without Triton: dtype acceptance; the QSA and state backends pack the int8
per-token-head spec like TRITON_ATTN (520 B cells, page = block x nkv x 520)
and leave bf16/fp8 specs untouched; qsa_pth_kv_views equals TRITON_ATTN's
scale views on HND, NHD and padded-page caches and writes no byte; the impl
accepts the dtype and rebuilds views after the runner's reset; the kernels'
scale placement vs an fp32 dense reference.

With TRITON_INTERPRET=1 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES= (the Triton kernels on CPU
tensors): Triton writer -> attn2 and split-K vs the dequantized reference and
vs the bf16 cache; bf16 launches unchanged; fused prepare int8 bytes/scales
equal the writer formula; unfused update ignores padded rows. The module
patches the Triton 3.8 interpreter's bf16 dot and int<->bf16 casts (it works
on raw uint16 bits there); compiled kernels are unaffected.

Result (GPUs masked): 34 passed (interpreter), 148 passed / 155
skipped with the existing QSA and IP CPU suites.
